@page "/cart"
@inject CartState Cart

<PageTitle>Memo</PageTitle>

<h1>Memo <RenderCount Value="++_renders" /></h1>
<p class="lead">
    <code>Memo</code> caches a computed property of a <code>[ReactiveState]</code> class without declaring a
    <code>Derived&lt;T&gt;</code> field. It is recomputed once when what it read changes, however many components
    read it, and its readers re-render only when the result differs.
</p>

<p>
    This cart's state uses each kind of computed property: <code>ItemCount</code> is a plain getter, cheap enough to
    run on every read. <code>Subtotal</code> is a memo over the cart lines, <code>Total</code> a memo that reads
    <code>Subtotal</code> and the discount, and <code>FreeShipping</code> a memo over <code>Total</code> whose result
    rarely changes. A memo can take a lambda, or a static lambda that receives the state, which reads without
    allocating; both behave the same.
</p>

<div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
        <h2>Cart</h2>
        <CartLinesView />
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Totals</h2>
        <CartTotals />
        <DiscountEditor />
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Shipping</h2>
        <ShippingBadge />
    </div>
</div>

<h2>Cached vs uncached readers</h2>
<p class="hint">
    Three components read the memo <code>FreeShipping</code> and three read <code>UncachedFreeShipping</code>, a plain
    getter with the same check. Change a quantity or the discount without crossing
    @CartState.FreeShippingThreshold.ToString("C"): only the plain getter readers re-render. Refresh the counts to
    compare computations.
</p>

<div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
        <h2>Memo readers</h2>
        <ShippingReader Cached="true" />
        <ShippingReader Cached="true" />
        <ShippingReader Cached="true" />
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Plain getter readers</h2>
        <ShippingReader Cached="false" />
        <ShippingReader Cached="false" />
        <ShippingReader Cached="false" />
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Computations</h2>
        <RunCounts />
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private int _renders;
}
